      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed substitution fraction is approximately 30–50% of the Hf content.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Hf with Nb will reduce the alloy density.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Hf with Nb will preserve strength at room temperature and approximately 1000 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-to-Nb substitution will retain a single-phase BCC solid-solution microstructure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb is significantly lighter than Hf.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb has a high melting point.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb has bonding characteristics compatible with HfMoTaTiZr that enable similar solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain sufficient lattice distortion to sustain high strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature phase stability and high melting temperatures support elevated-temperature strength in refractory high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy is expected to have a 5–10% lower density than as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Room-temperature compressive strength and approximately 1000 °C yield strength will remain comparable to, or within 10% of, the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed operating boundary extends from room temperature to approximately 1000 °C under similar mechanical loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The result may not translate to temperatures above 1200 °C or to different processing conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled series with 0%, 30%, 50%, and 70% replacement of Hf by Nb can test the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
